Configuration and uninstall boundary
------------------------------------
The installed application keeps configuration, trusted devices, and transfer
history outside the installation directory. A normal upgrade or uninstall does
not delete that user data. Reinstalling the same product can reuse it.

The portable archive is intentionally different: its settings directory stays
beside the executable and is removed when the portable folder is deleted.

Internal package signature
--------------------------
This package is unsigned unless both its file name and artifact manifest say it
is signed. An unsigned internal package remains usable for development and
testing, but Windows may display an unknown-publisher warning.
